<v Mark Gediman>It came to the point where every record company thought that the other record company was going to sign me. And, in effect, that I was going to be the next big thing. There were articles written saying that I was going to be the next Kiss, and this, and that. And Warner Brothers, they were going to have cartoons. And even where they were talking about designing some sort of video pinball game, a real total marketing thing.
<v Mark Gediman>到了后来，每家唱片公司都以为对方会签下我。实际上，我即将成为下一个大红大紫的明星。当时报纸上写着我将成为下一个Kiss乐队，云云。华纳兄弟甚至考虑要做卡通片。他们甚至讨论过设计某种视频弹球游戏，完全是商业营销那一套。

00:24:26.440 --> 00:25:01.670
<v Mark Gediman>And I was so excited. And we were a couple of weeks away from signing the contract when OPEC had a oil embargo in 1979. The price of plastic went up 400%. And that was the end of my shot right there. It just vanished before my eyes.
<v Mark Gediman>我当时兴奋极了。我们离签署合同只有几周时间了，结果1979年爆发了OPEC石油危机。塑料价格上涨了400%。我的机会在那一刻直接终结了。它就在我眼前消失了。

